  "jobTitle": "Web Developer, Web Designer",
  "summary": "I am a web and digital interface designer and front-end developer specializing in fast, accessible, standards-compliant websites for businesses, nonprofits, and public agencies. \n\nMy work addresses the problems that most often undermine small organization websites: slow performance on real-world connections, barriers for keyboard and assistive technology users, and unclear ownership of domains, hosting, and code. Every project is built mobile-first and evaluated against WCAG 2.2 AA. \n\nTechnical focus: HTML5, CSS3, JavaScript (ES6+), and PHP, including the back-end functionality that supports the interface, such as forms, data handling, and authentication. I also build on WordPress, other CMS platforms, and site builders when they best fit a client’s needs. \n\nExperience includes: municipal and civic website redesigns, e-commerce, small business sites, accessibility audits and remediation, performance and security improvements, and site recovery for organizations that lost access to their own website. I have a particular focus on ADA Title II web accessibility requirements for city and county governments. \n\nEducation: A.A.S. in Media Design Technology, Pellissippi State Community College (cum laude, Phi Theta Kappa), with certificates in Webpage Authoring, Mobile-First Web Design, and E-Commerce Web Design. \n\nHC Web Labs is based in Rocky Top, Tennessee, serving East Tennessee organizations in person and clients nationwide remotely. \n\nTo request a complimentary website review: webmaster@heather-cooper.com",
